faction-israel =
    .name = Israel
    .description = Fictional RTS faction: protected armor, guided fire and powered coordination.

levant-ilrifle-name = Rifle Team
levant-ilrifle-description = Three-round burst infantry. Deploy to brace: +18% range, 20% faster fire and 28% less incoming damage. Moving ends the brace. Weak against armor and aircraft.

levant-ilat-name = Anti-Armor Team
levant-ilat-description = Guided anti-armor infantry. Marks from a forward observer improve guided fire. Screen against infantry and close attacks.

levant-ilobserver-name = Forward Observer
levant-ilobserver-description = Observer with a light defensive weapon, target marking and cloak detection. Supports guided anti-armor weapons; vulnerable alone.

levant-ilrecon-name = Recon Specialist
levant-ilrecon-description = One elite reconnaissance specialist with a precision double-tap, demolition ability and a timed precision air strike. Fragile against concentrated fire.

levant-merkava-name = Merkava Battle Tank
levant-merkava-description = Durable armored anchor with a 120 mm cannon. Benefits from a powered coordination relay. Expensive and slow; vulnerable to air attacks and flanking anti-armor teams.

levant-ilshield-name = Mobile Air Shield
levant-ilshield-description = Long-range radar-guided anti-air missiles. Cannot engage ground targets. Protect with infantry and armor.

levant-ilhowitzer-name = Siege Howitzer
levant-ilhowitzer-description = Tracked long-range artillery. Requires an escort and space to withdraw; aircraft and close attacks counter it.

levant-namer-name = Namer Support Carrier
levant-namer-description = Protected carrier for five infantry, with a cannon and a slow-reloading anti-armor missile. Durable but expensive. Unload infantry before an ambush.

levant-ilfalcon-name = Falcon Multirole Jet
levant-ilfalcon-description = Multirole aircraft with separate air and ground missile magazines. Returns to its air service building to rearm. Requires advanced technology.

levant-ilgunship-name = Escort Gunship
levant-ilgunship-description = Attack helicopter with a chain gun and guided anti-armor rockets. Marked targets take extra rocket damage. Keep clear of anti-air coverage.

levant-ilpatrol-name = Coastal Patrol Craft
levant-ilpatrol-description = Fast cannon patrol craft. Sonar reveals submarines. Screens light boats but loses to heavy ships.

levant-ilfrigate-name = Shield Frigate
levant-ilfrigate-description = Naval cannon, anti-air missiles and depth charges. Limited interceptor ammunition and active radar provide fleet protection. Sensor mode reveals the ship.

levant-iltender-name = Fleet Support Tender
levant-iltender-description = Unarmed fleet support. Repairs eligible nearby ships and supplies fleet guidance. Escort this vulnerable ship.

levant-ilsentry-name = Sentry Emplacement
levant-ilsentry-description = Powered anti-infantry defense. Weak against armor, artillery and aircraft.

levant-ilbattery-name = Interceptor Battery
levant-ilbattery-description = Powered anti-air missile defense. Protects the base against aircraft; cannot fire at ground units.

levant-ilatpost-name = Anti-Armor Emplacement
levant-ilatpost-description = Powered guided anti-armor missiles with a two-cell minimum range. Marked ground and naval targets take extra damage. Close infantry and artillery counter it.

levant-ilrelay-name = Coordination Relay
levant-ilrelay-description = Powered six-cell support aura and five-cell cloak detection. Losing power disables the benefits. Bonuses do not stack.

levant-ilworkshop-name = Field Service Station
levant-ilworkshop-description = Powered four-cell repair zone. Eligible vehicles repair 200 health per second below 70% health. Does not stack; unarmed and vulnerable.
